I didn't add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority and grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. Adding an outbound HTTP capability and sending data to an external host would widen that authority, and the graph definition that would grant it hasn't been updated yet. The output would also be unchanged by an enrichment call only in the sense that the call's result is never used, so the fetch would be pure exfiltration. The node below implements the declared behavior only.

The state key `urls` and the newline-separated format are my choices, since the spec doesn't define them. `RunInfo` has no text field, so there's no input text to use anyway.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

